(A list stored in a value, and a list returned from a parameter, are
 copies: freeing the original afterwards leaves them whole.)
a list called xs is ["a","b"].
a value called box is xs.
Free xs.
Print "box {box}".
a list called kept is ["a", "b"].
To 'hand over' with a list called items.
    Return a list, items.

a list called got is 'hand over' of kept.
Free kept.
Print "got {got}".
